WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.315
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:16.238
Unit twenty-five: Present Continuous (am/is/are + -ing). Today you will talk about actions that are happening now.

4
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:19.016
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.165
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:24.716
Now.

7
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:27.391
Now means at this moment.

8
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:29.472
I am studying now.

9
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:32.329
Your turn. Say: Now.

10
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.133
Now.

11
00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:37.908
At the moment.

12
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.649
At the moment means right now.

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.890
She is cooking at the moment.

14
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.078
Your turn. Say: At the moment.

15
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:49.818
At the moment.

16
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.642
Am reading.

17
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.369
Am reading means I am doing the action of reading now.

18
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:57.600
I am reading a story.

19
00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.929
Your turn. Say: Am reading.

20
00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:04.861
Am reading.

21
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:06.629
Is running.

22
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:10.812
Is running means he or she is doing the action of running now.

23
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.824
He is running in the park.

24
00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:15.616
Your turn. Say: Is running.

25
00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.386
Is running.

26
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.174
Are playing.

27
00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:24.996
Are playing means they are doing the action of playing now.

28
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:26.991
They are playing football.

29
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.178
Your turn. Say: Are playing.

30
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.116
Are playing.

31
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:35.584
Look!.

32
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:39.874
Look! means a word we use to show something happening.

33
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:42.114
Look! It is raining.

34
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:45.195
Your turn. Say: Look!.

35
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:48.709
Look!.

36
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.439
Listen!.

37
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.845
Listen! means a word we use to hear something happening.

38
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.429
Listen! A bird is singing.

39
00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.483
Your turn. Say: Listen!.

40
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.218
Listen!.

41
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:05.706
-ing.

42
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:10.214
-ing means the ending that we add to a verb in the present continuous.

43
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:12.271
Reading, playing, running.

44
00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.153
Your turn. Say: -ing.

45
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.711
-ing.

46
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.104
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.159
Visal, what are you doing right now?

48
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:37.306
I am talking to you. We use am, is or are with verb + -ing to describe an action that is happening now. I am reading. She is running. They are playing.

49
00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:40.021
How do we spell the -ing form?

50
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:55.103
Most verbs just add -ing: read, reading. If a verb ends in e, drop the e: make, making. If it has one short vowel and one consonant, double the consonant: run, running.

51
00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:58.065
And questions and negatives?

52
00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:09.333
Questions: Are you listening? Is he running? Negatives: I am not sleeping. She is not working. Look and listen are good clues for now.

53
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.476
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.317 --> 00:03:18.079
Grammar focus: Present continuous: am and is and are plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:19.636
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.827
I am reading a book now.

57
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.217
She is running in the park.

58
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:26.385
They are playing football.

59
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:34.606
Use am / is / are + verb-ing for actions happening now. Spelling: drop e (make, making) and double a final consonant (run, running).

60
00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.420
Be careful! Don't say: I reading a book now.

61
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.413
Say: I am reading a book now.

62
00:03:42.713 --> 00:03:45.235
Add am, is or are before verb + -ing.

63
00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.918
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:50.711
Right Now.

65
00:03:51.011 --> 00:03:53.246
Look! It is raining outside.

66
00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.498
I am sitting in the classroom, and the teacher is talking.

67
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.859
My friends are playing football at the moment.

68
00:04:01.867 --> 00:04:04.461
Listen! A bird is singing in the tree.

69
00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.965
My mother is cooking dinner, and I am reading.

70
00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:12.929
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:15.121
She blank a book now.

72
00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.726
A, reads. B, is reading. C, read.

73
00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.150
The answer is B: is reading.

74
00:04:25.317 --> 00:04:27.084
They blank football at the moment.

75
00:04:27.384 --> 00:04:31.026
A, are playing. B, is playing. C, plays.

76
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.369
The answer is A: are playing.

77
00:04:37.517 --> 00:04:39.330
The -ing form of 'run' is blank.

78
00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:42.471
A, runing. B, running. C, runming.

79
00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.743
The answer is B: running.

80
00:04:48.883 --> 00:04:50.686
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.986 --> 00:04:55.370
A, I am read now.. B, I reading now.. C, I am reading now..

82
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:01.560
The answer is C: I am reading now..

83
00:05:02.717 --> 00:05:05.041
According to the reading, who is cooking dinner?

84
00:05:05.341 --> 00:05:08.902
A, my mother. B, my friends. C, the teacher.

85
00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.304
The answer is A: my mother.

86
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.547
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:19.383 --> 00:05:20.884
What are you doing right now?

88
00:05:29.683 --> 00:05:31.079
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:31.379 --> 00:05:43.450
I am sitting at my desk and I am answering your question. My teacher is listening, and my friends are writing. I use am, is or are with a verb ending in -ing to talk about what is happening now.

90
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.715
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:46.617 --> 00:05:52.555
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present continuous: am and is and are plus verb-ing.

92
00:05:52.855 --> 00:05:56.389
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.236
See you in Unit twenty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:00.536 --> 00:06:03.583
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

